{"paper": true, "state": "live", "as_of_session": "2026-09-25", "book": "MAIN", "withheld_total_eur": 0.0, "by_year": [], "credits": [], "credits_total_eur": 0, "earliest_expiry": null, "expired_total_eur": 0, "deferred_tax_eur": 0.0, "pre_tax_eq": 10000.0, "after_tax_eq": 10000.0, "div_not_credited_eur": 0.0, "div_ex_dates": 0, "whole_share_residual_eur": 0.0, "whole_share_residual_avg_eur": null, "sales": [], "rules": ["Every book keeps an Italian tax ledger, as a broker does under the regime amministrato: 26% of each realised gain on shares is withheld from the book's cash at the sale (D.Lgs. 461/97 art. 6 c.9).", "Gain = sale proceeds − purchase cost; both €1 fees reduce the gain (TUIR art. 68 c.6). The Italian transaction tax is not deductible (L. 228/2012); the lab does not deduct the French and Spanish ones either (not verified; the cautious side).", "A loss becomes a credit against later gains in the same year and the next four (art. 6 c.5), used oldest first; tax already withheld is never refunded. A credit from year Y lapses at the start of the first session of Y + 5.", "The Europe ETF (X1) follows the fund rule: the gain is capital income, taxed at 26% with no deductions and not offset by credits; its losses and fees become credits.", "Sales in the same session are booked in ISIN order: the lab has no execution times. A real investor who sold the losing position first could pay slightly less tax that evening.", "PRE-TAX = the book with the withheld tax added back. AFTER-TAX = the book less the tax that selling everything that evening would withhold. Neither deducts the exit fees or spread of that sale.", "Today's rules are applied to all of history (the rate was 12.5% before 2012 and 20% from 2012 to 30 June 2014)."], "all_books": [{"book": "R1", "withheld_total_eur": 0.0, "credits_total_eur": 0, "earliest_expiry": null, "expired_total_eur": 0, "deferred_tax_eur": 0.0, "div_not_credited_eur": 0.0, "whole_share_residual_eur": 0.0}, {"book": "R2", "withheld